The `removeNthFromEnd` method takes in the head of a singly linked list and an integer `n`, representing the position of the node to be removed from the end of the list. The method should remove the nth node from the end of the list and return the head of the modified list. Assume 1 ≤ n ≤ length of the list.

For example, given the linked list `1 -> 2 -> 3 -> 4 -> 5` and `n = 2`, the method should modify the list to `1 -> 2 -> 3 -> 5` and return the head of the modified list.

